WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.767
-A lot of fans are theorizing
that this Friday

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:05.467
Taylor Swift is going to drop
"1989 (Taylor's version),"

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:07.367
and could also release --
[ Cheering ]

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:09.167
could also release
"Speak Now (Taylor's Version)"

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:11.367
on the same day.

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:14.534
-Yeah, but how do you know that?
Isn't that just a rumor?

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:17.601
-[ Scoffs ] The clues are
everywhere, Tariq.

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:18.934
-What clues?

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:21.467
-Okay, so in Taylor's last music
video for the "Red" --

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:23.167
for Red (Taylor's Version)"
bonus track

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:24.934
"I Bet You Think It's About Me,"
there's a wedding cake.

00:00:24.934 --> 00:00:27.300
And on the cake there are
numbers 13 and 26.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.767
You follow?

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:31.067
-Yeah, no.
-Uh, "Red (Taylor's version)"

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:32.567
was Taylor's most
recent re-release.

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:35.067
13 is Taylor's favorite number,
and this Friday, May 13th

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:36.701
is 26 weeks
from the release date

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:38.367
of "Red (Taylor's version)."

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:40.234
-Okay, well, I guess --

00:00:40.234 --> 00:00:42.334
-Also if you look at Taylor's
official store,

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:44.234
signed CD copies of
"Fearless (Taylor's version)"

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:46.968
are currently on sale
for $19.89.

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:50.601
Get it?
1989, 1989!

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:51.834
-Alright.
Well, then you're probably --

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:53.400
-But also,
"Red (Taylor's version)"

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.634
was listed on sale
on her store for $20.10

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:57.634
in purple text.

00:00:57.634 --> 00:00:58.934
-And that means what?

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:00.234
-Are you even listening?

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:02.200
The original "Speak Now"
was released in 2010,

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.100
and the cover of that album,
she's wearing a purple dress.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:07.000
Purple, 2010, $20.10!

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:10.634
And six days ago, after dropping
her newest single,

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:12.567
"This Love (Taylor's version),"
which is a song originally

00:01:12.567 --> 00:01:14.901
from "1989," she wrote
on Instagram that she

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:16.434
"reliving the '1989' tour."

00:01:16.434 --> 00:01:17.767
But she also put a bunch
of merch called

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:20.000
"The old Taylor Collection"
that features clothes

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.467
referencing both "1989"
and "Speak Now."

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:23.200
I mean, it can't be
any more obvious.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:27.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:30.834
-You --

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:33.234
You know you're 47 years old,
right?

00:01:33.234 --> 00:01:35.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:37.501
-Yeah, but I'm 47,
Jimmy's version.

